:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CHGOUTQ.Change Output Queue (CHGOUTQ)
:P.Use the Change Output Queue (CHGOUTQ) command to change the
attributes of an output queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/MAXPAGES'.Maximum spooled file size (MAXPAGES)
:P.The maximum spooled file size for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pages
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. End time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 235959 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/AUTOSTRWTR'.Writers to autostart (AUTOSTRWTR)
:P.The writers to autostart for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/DSPDTA'.Display any file (DSPDTA)
:P.The display any file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/JOBSEP'.Job separators (JOBSEP)
:P.The job separators for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/OPRCTL'.Operator controlled (OPRCTL)
:P.Whether users with job control special authority can control the
queue.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/DTAQ'.Data queue (DTAQ)
:P.The data queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/AUTCHK'.Authority to check (AUTCHK)
:P.Which authority is checked&colon. the owner's, or data authority.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAAUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/SEQ'.Order of files on queue (SEQ)
:P.The order of files on queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FIFO:EPK.
:PD.First in, first out.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBNBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/RMTPRTQ'.Remote printer queue (RMTPRTQ)
:P.The remote printer queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/CNNTYPE'.Connection type (CNNTYPE)
:P.The connection type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SNA:EPK.
:PD.SNA.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IPX, *USRDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/DESTTYPE'.Destination type (DESTTYPE)
:P.The destination type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*OTHER:EPK.
:PD.Other.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OS400, *OS400V2, *PSF2, *S390, *NDS, *NETWARE3,
*NETWARE4.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/VMMVSCLASS'.VM/MVS class (VMMVSCLASS)
:P.The VM/MVS class for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/FCB'.Forms control buffer (FCB)
:P.The forms control buffer for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USRDTA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/TRANSFORM'.Transform SCS to ASCII (TRANSFORM)
:P.Whether the host print transform converts the SCS data to the
printer's ASCII data stream.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WSCST, *IBM42011, *HPLJ4, *HP4, *HP5SI,
*IBM3812, *IBM4019, *IBM4029, *IBM4039HP, *IBM5577, *IBMPAGES,
*LEXOPTRA, *NECP2, *PRESTIGE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/WSCST'.Workstation customizing (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/DESTOPT'.Destination options (DESTOPT)
:P.Options passed to the remote system that receives the spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/USRDFNOPT'.User defined options (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/USRDTATFM'.User data transform (USRDTATFM)
:P.The program that transforms the user data of a spooled file before it
is sent to the printer.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/MSGQ'.Queue for writer messages (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/SEPPAGE'.Print separator page (SEPPAGE)
:P.Whether a separator page prints before each spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOUTQ/USRDRVPGM'.User driver program (USRDRVPGM)
:P.The user driver program that sends spooled files when no device
writer is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSPLFA.Change Spooled File Attr (CHGSPLFA)
:P.Use the Change Spooled File Attr (CHGSPLFA) command to change the
attributes of a spooled file, or of the files SELECT picks when
FILE(*SELECT) is given.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/SELECT'.Select files for (SELECT)
:P.The select files for for this command.
:P.The value has 5 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. User
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Print device
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Form type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. User data
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 5&colon. ASP
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASPDEV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/PRTDEV'.Printer (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FORMTYPE'.Form type (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/COPIES'.Copies (COPIES)
:P.How many copies are printed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/RESTART'.Restart printing (RESTART)
:P.The restart printing for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NEXT:EPK.
:PD.The next one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STRPAGE, *ENDPAGE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/PAGERANGE'.Page range to print (PAGERANGE)
:P.The page range to print for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start page
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End page
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/OUTPTY'.Output priority (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FILESEP'.File separators (FILESEP)
:P.How many separator pages print before each spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/SCHEDULE'.Spooled output schedule (SCHEDULE)
:P.When the spooled file can begin to print&colon. as soon as it is
created, when it is closed, or when the job ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/SAVE'.Save file (SAVE)
:P.The save file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/OUTBIN'.Output bin (OUTBIN)
:P.The output bin the printed pages go to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/PRTQLTY'.Print quality (PRTQLTY)
:P.The print quality&colon. draft, normal text or near-letter quality.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DRAFT:EPK.
:PD.Draft quality.
:PT.:PK.*NLQ:EPK.
:PD.Near letter quality.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FASTDRAFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FORMFEED'.Form feed (FORMFEED)
:P.How paper is fed to the printer&colon. continuous forms, cut sheets
fed by hand, or an automatic sheet feeder.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CONT:EPK.
:PD.Continuous forms.
:PT.:PK.*CUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets fed by hand.
:PT.:PK.*AUTOCUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets from a sheet feeder.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONT2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/DRAWER'.Source drawer (DRAWER)
:P.The paper drawer the output is printed from.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *E1, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FONT'.Font (FONT)
:P.The font the printer uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CPI:EPK.
:PD.Characters per inch.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CPI:EPK.
:PD.Characters per inch.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Point size
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.1 to 999.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/ALIGN'.Align page (ALIGN)
:P.Whether the writer stops on the first page so the forms can be
aligned.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/USRDTA'.User data (USRDTA)
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/PAGDFN'.Page definition (PAGDFN)
:P.The page definition for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/FORMDF'.Form definition (FORMDF)
:P.The form definition for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/USRDFNOPT'.User defined options (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/EXPDATE'.Expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DAYS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSPLFA/DAYS'.Days to keep file (DAYS)
:P.The days to keep file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 366.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGWTR.Change Writer (CHGWTR)
:P.Use the Change Writer (CHGWTR) command to change the attributes of a
started writer.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/WTR'.Writer (WTR)
:P.The writer&colon. the job that prints the spooled files of an output
queue.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/FORMTYPE'.Form type options (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Form type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FORMS.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Message option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INQMSG, *NOMSG, *INFOMSG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/FILESEP'.File separators (FILESEP)
:P.How many separator pages print before each spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/SEPDRAWER'.Drawer for separators (SEPDRAWER)
:P.The drawer for separators for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGWTR/OPTION'.When to change writer (OPTION)
:P.The when to change writer for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ANYRDYF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLROUTQ.Clear Output Queue (CLROUTQ)
:P.Use the Clear Output Queue (CLROUTQ) command to delete every spooled
file on an output queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLROUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYSPLF.Copy Spooled File (CPYSPLF)
:P.Use the Copy Spooled File (CPYSPLF) command to copy a spooled file
into a database file member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/TOFILE'.To database file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/TOMBR'.To member (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/CTLCHAR'.Control character (CTLCHAR)
:P.The control characters in the data&colon. none, or the first
character of each record as a FORTRAN control character.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FCFC:EPK.
:PD.The first character of each record is a FORTRAN forms control
character.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRTCTL, *S36FMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/CHLVAL'.Channel values (CHLVAL)
:P.The lines of the page that channels 1 to 12 skip to.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Channel number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 12.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Line numbers
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/WSCST'.Workstation customizing (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSPLF/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTOUTQ.Create Output Queue (CRTOUTQ)
:P.Use the Create Output Queue (CRTOUTQ) command to create an output
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/MAXPAGES'.Maximum spooled file size (MAXPAGES)
:P.The maximum spooled file size for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pages
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. End time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 235959 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/AUTOSTRWTR'.Writers to autostart (AUTOSTRWTR)
:P.The writers to autostart for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/DSPDTA'.Display any file (DSPDTA)
:P.The display any file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/JOBSEP'.Job separators (JOBSEP)
:P.The job separators for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/OPRCTL'.Operator controlled (OPRCTL)
:P.Whether users with job control special authority can control the
queue.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/DTAQ'.Data queue (DTAQ)
:P.The data queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/AUTCHK'.Authority to check (AUTCHK)
:P.Which authority is checked&colon. the owner's, or data authority.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAAUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/SEQ'.Order of files on queue (SEQ)
:P.The order of files on queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIFO:EPK.
:PD.First in, first out.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBNBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/RMTPRTQ'.Remote printer queue (RMTPRTQ)
:P.The remote printer queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/CNNTYPE'.Connection type (CNNTYPE)
:P.The connection type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNA:EPK.
:PD.SNA.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IPX, *USRDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/DESTTYPE'.Destination type (DESTTYPE)
:P.The destination type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OTHER:EPK.
:PD.Other.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OS400, *OS400V2, *PSF2, *S390, *NDS, *NETWARE3,
*NETWARE4.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/VMMVSCLASS'.VM/MVS class (VMMVSCLASS)
:P.The VM/MVS class for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, A is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/FCB'.Forms control buffer (FCB)
:P.The forms control buffer for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USRDTA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/TRANSFORM'.Transform SCS to ASCII (TRANSFORM)
:P.Whether the host print transform converts the SCS data to the
printer's ASCII data stream.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WSCST, *IBM42011, *HPLJ4, *HP4, *HP5SI,
*IBM3812, *IBM4019, *IBM4029, *IBM4039HP, *IBM5577, *IBMPAGES,
*LEXOPTRA, *NECP2, *PRESTIGE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/WSCST'.Workstation customizing (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/DESTOPT'.Destination options (DESTOPT)
:P.Options passed to the remote system that receives the spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/USRDFNOPT'.User defined options (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/USRDTATFM'.User data transform (USRDTATFM)
:P.The program that transforms the user data of a spooled file before it
is sent to the printer.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/SPLFASP'.Spooled file ASP (SPLFASP)
:P.The spooled file ASP for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OUTQASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/ASPDEV'.Spooled file ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OUTQASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/MSGQ'.Queue for writer messages (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYSOPR is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/SEPPAGE'.Print separator page (SEPPAGE)
:P.Whether a separator page prints before each spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTOUTQ/USRDRVPGM'.User driver program (USRDRVPGM)
:P.The user driver program that sends spooled files when no device
writer is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTOUTQ.Delete Output Queue (DLTOUTQ)
:P.Use the Delete Output Queue (DLTOUTQ) command to delete an output
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTOUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTSPLF.Delete Spooled File (DLTSPLF)
:P.Use the Delete Spooled File (DLTSPLF) command to delete a spooled
file, or the files SELECT picks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTSPLF/SELECT'.Select files for (SELECT)
:P.The select files for for this command.
:P.The value has 5 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. User
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Print device
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Form type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. User data
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 5&colon. ASP
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASPDEV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSPLF.Display Spooled File (DSPSPLF)
:P.Use the Display Spooled File (DSPSPLF) command to show the contents
of a spooled file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
