:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/CTLCHAR'.Control character (CTLCHAR)
:P.The control characters in the data&colon. none, or the first
character of each record as a FORTRAN control character.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FCFC:EPK.
:PD.The first character of each record is a FORTRAN forms control
character.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRTCTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSPLF/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDWTR.End Writer (ENDWTR)
:P.Use the End Writer (ENDWTR) command to end a spooling writer.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDWTR/WTR'.Writer (WTR)
:P.The writer&colon. the job that prints the spooled files of an output
queue.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDWTR/OPTION'.When to end writer (OPTION)
:P.The when to end writer for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PAGEEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLDOUTQ.Hold Output Queue (HLDOUTQ)
:P.Use the Hold Output Queue (HLDOUTQ) command to hold an output queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDOUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLDSPLF.Hold Spooled File (HLDSPLF)
:P.Use the Hold Spooled File (HLDSPLF) command to hold a spooled file,
or the files SELECT picks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDSPLF/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDSPLF/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDSPLF/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDSPLF/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
