:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPRTWTR/AUTOEND'.Automatically end writer (AUTOEND)
:P.The automatically end writer for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. End writer
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. When to end
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NORDYF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPRTWTR/ALIGN'.Forms alignment (ALIGN)
:P.Whether the writer stops on the first page so the forms can be
aligned.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WTR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRRMTWTR.Start Remote Writer (STRRMTWTR)
:P.Use the Start Remote Writer (STRRMTWTR) command to start a writer
that sends an output queue to a remote system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRRMTWTR/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRRMTWTR/MSGQ'.Queue for writer messages (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRRMTWTR/FORMTYPE'.Form type options (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Form type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FORMS.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Message option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOMSG, *INQMSG, *INFOMSG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRRMTWTR/WTR'.Writer (WTR)
:P.The writer&colon. the job that prints the spooled files of an output
queue.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PK.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRRMTWTR/AUTOEND'.Auto-end options (AUTOEND)
:P.The auto-end options for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
