:H4.Part 1&colon. Automatically end writer
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. If yes, when to end
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NORDYF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOUTQ.Work with Output Queue (WRKOUTQ)
:P.Use the Work with Output Queue (WRKOUTQ) command to list output
queues, or the spooled files of one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOUTQ/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOUTQ/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOUTQD.Work with Output Queue Desc (WRKOUTQD)
:P.Use the Work with Output Queue Desc (WRKOUTQD) command to show the
description of an output queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOUTQD/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
