printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSPLF.Work with Spooled Files (WRKSPLF)
:P.Use the Work with Spooled Files (WRKSPLF) command to list spooled
files and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/SELECT'.Select files for (SELECT)
:P.The select files for for this command.
:P.The value has 6 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. User
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Print device
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Form type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. User data
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 5&colon. ASP
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASPDEV.
:H4.Part 6&colon. ASP device
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/PERIOD'.Time period (PERIOD)
:P.The time period for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BEGIN.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. End time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
